From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0293: AppleKeyStore: aks_wrap_key hands back the key class it was given

libaks calls aks_wrap_key with two scalars, the keybag handle and the key class; the class goes
back as the wrapped key's actual class. The wrap handed back the first scalar, the handle (0), so
securityd recorded every new keychain item, and every metadata key, as class 0. Reading an item
back then found no metadata key for class 0, the item was called corrupt (-26275 "Unable to find a
suitable metadata key") and deleted: nothing written to the keychain survived its first read, so
Wi-Fi passwords (and every app's keychain data) were lost. The class is now the second scalar.
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
index 43960bd..2f7b8f0 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetKeyStore.cpp
@@ -956,9 +956,17 @@ sweet_aks_wrap(IOExternalMethodArguments *args, bool wrap)
 	bzero(in, sizeof(in));
 	bzero(out, sizeof(out));
 	if (ret == kIOReturnSuccess) {
-		/* wrap: the key's class back (the one asked for); unwrap: nothing */
+		/*
+		 * wrap: the key's class back (the one asked for); unwrap: nothing.
+		 * 0293: libaks passes (keybag handle, key class): the class is the second scalar. Handing
+		 * back the first (the handle, 0) made securityd record every new item and metadata key as
+		 * class 0; reading one back then found no metadata key for class 0, called the item corrupt
+		 * (-26275) and deleted it: nothing written to the keychain survived its first read, Wi-Fi
+		 * passwords included.
+		 */
 		if (wrap && args->scalarOutputCount >= 1) {
-			args->scalarOutput[0] = args->scalarInputCount > 0 ? args->scalarInput[0] : 0;
+			args->scalarOutput[0] = args->scalarInputCount > 1 ? args->scalarInput[1] :
+			    (args->scalarInputCount > 0 ? args->scalarInput[0] : 0);
 			args->scalarOutputCount = 1;
 		} else {
 			args->scalarOutputCount = 0;
